### Why this plan

The assessment found that `scripts/preseed_session_plan.py --test` fails because `_check_code_already_exists()` finds task keywords in the planning script's own constant definitions and test data — falsely declaring every task "already done." This is the most likely root cause of `planner_no_task_count` and the Day 145-147 empty streak. Task_01 fixes that directly.

Task_02 adds a safety net: when no candidates match, prefer a verifiable `src/state.rs` task over a self-referential "fix the planner" task. Combined with task_01, this gives the pipeline two layers of defense against empty sessions.

Task_03 addresses the trajectory's `deepseek_model_call_abnormal_completed_count=2` by making zero-token model responses self-documenting — future traces will show *why* the model returned empty.

